ter."}, {"id": "oyster", "sp": "crassostrea virginica", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "Filters algae from the water. Wikipedia notes oysters face more disease under hypoxia.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "worms", "sp": "polychaetes and bivalves", "xh": 0.58}, {"id": "shrimp", "sp": "farfantepenaeus aztecus", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "croaker", "sp": "micropogonias undulatus", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "trout", "sp": "cynoscion nebulosus", "xh": 0.26}, {"id": "redsnapper", "sp": "lutjanus campechanus", "xh": 0.4}, {"id": "redfish", "sp": "sciaenops ocellatus", "xh": 0.52}, {"id": "crab", "sp": "callinectes sapidus", "xh": 0.63, "desc": "An omnivore that eats oysters, worms and carrion.", "ic": "ant"}, {"id": "jelly", "sp": "chrysaora quinquecirrha", "xh": 0.72, "desc": "A jellyfish. Wikipedia says jellyfish can survive hypoxia and may increase when competitors and predators leave."}, {"id": "turtle", "sp": "lepidochelys kempii", "xh": 0.83}, {"id": "pelican", "sp": "pelecanus erythrorhynchos", "xh": 0.94}, {"id": "dolphin", "sp": "tursiops truncatus", "xh": 0.3, "wiki": "Bottlenose dolphin", "desc": "Eats fish, shrimp and squid, often herding schools toward shore. Large sharks including bull sharks prey on it."}, {"id": "bullshark", "sp": "carcharhinus leucas", "xh": 0.68}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "Warm, bright surface water lets blooms grow fast in summer."}, {"id": "plume", "sp": "river nutrients", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "oxygen", "sp": "bottom-water oxygen", "xh": 0.64, "desc": "Warm, layered water traps oxygen-poor water near the bottom. Bottom dwellers that cannot leave suffocate when oxygen falls very low."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.88, "name": "Bacteria", "desc": "Break down dead algae. In summer this uses up bottom-water oxygen and creates the dead zone."}], "raw": [["sun", "phyto", "r"], ["sun", "spartina", "r"], ["plume", "phyto", "r"], ["plume", "spartina", "r"], ["oxygen", "worms", "r"], ["oxygen", "oyster", "r"], ["oxygen", 